466 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 465 0 R
  /Alt (This image is a screenshot of a user profile page within the CLC+ (CORINE Land Cover Plus) Core administrative interface, part of the Copernicus Land Monitoring Service (CLMS) and European Environment Agency (EEA) EAGLE framework. The page is titled 'User 'CLC+ Core User Admin/Support'' and shows an 'ACTIVE' status badge. Action buttons to the right are 'DEACTIVATE' and 'EDIT'. The page is divided into three sections: 1. **General Information:** * EIONET Username: `clccore` * Last name: `CLC+ Core` * First name: `User Admin/Support` * Organisation/s: `CLC`, `European Environment Agency` * Email: `jaguilar@bilbomatica.es` * Status: `active` * A button labelled 'VISIT EIONET FOR CONTACT DETAILS' with an EIONET logo. 2. **Roles:** This section lists four distinct user roles with descriptions: * **Database Administrator:** 'For now, this role is only available within CLCplus Core so that it can be seen who is the database administrator. For later this role could be used for additional views like e.g., performance view.' * **EAGLE maintainer / Approver:** 'As an EAGLE maintainer you are allowed to add a new EAGLE ontology version to the CLCplus Core and approve EAGLE compliance of ingestions.' * **System Administrator:** 'For now, this role is only available within CLCplus Core so that it can be seen who is the system administrator. For later this role could be used for additional views like e.g., scheduling view.' * **User Administrator / Support:** 'As an User Administrator / Support you are allowed to manage (Add, Edit, Activate/Inactivate) users and organisations within the CLCplus Core. Additionally, you can view and edit any Ingestion and Extraction within the CLCplus Core in order to support users if they are in need of help.' 3. **Advanced options:** * '10 m processing' is displayed with a green toggle switch indicating it is currently enabled. This relates to the system's ability to process data at 10-metre resolution. The top navigation bar includes links for 'Data Catalogue', 'EAGLE Ontology', 'About EAGLE', 'Organisations', and 'Users', along with 'CLC+ Core User Admin/Support'. The footer displays logos for the European Union, Copernicus, EIONET Action Group EAGLE Land Monitoring in Europe, European Commission, and the European Environment Agency.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [10]
  /Pg 941 0 R
>>
